In the issue, focus is on an element outside the grid, for example the button that opens the select. Without that, this test fails on unfixed code only in Chromium. It passes in Firefox and WebKit, so it does not reproduce the bug there.

```suggestion
    // Focus stays outside the grid, e.g. on a button that opens the select
    fixtureSync('<button></button>').focus();
    select.opened = true;
```

CONVENTIONS.md: tests that move the pointer with `sendMouseToElement` must call `resetMouse()` in `afterEach`. The same applies to `dialog-grid.test.js`.

```js
afterEach(async () => {
  await resetMouse();
});
```

Assert the value as well, so the test proves that the click picked an item. For the spy, CONVENTIONS.md asks for sinon-chai matchers.

```suggestion
    expect(select.value).to.equal('2');
    expect(spy).to.not.be.called;
```

Markup shows the setup at a glance. Unlike `append`, it also does not add another popover each time the renderer runs.

```suggestion
      column.renderer = (root) => {
        root.innerHTML = '<div popover="manual">Popover</div>';
      };
```

This does not use `this`, so it can be a module-level function. Per CONVENTIONS.md, those need no `@private` tag or `__` prefix.

```js
const isInsideCellPopover = (event, cell) => {
  const path = event.composedPath();
  return path.slice(0, path.indexOf(cell)).some((node) => node.popover);
};
```
